course: dictionary
lesson: 11282
title: Writhing and wordplay
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Writhing means twisting and turning your body, usually because of pain, or wriggling like a snake or worm. Look at the clues around it. If a character is writhing on the ground, they are probably hurt, not dancing.
explain: Writhing can also mean feeling very embarrassed or upset, as in «writhing with embarrassment». Here the word describes a feeling inside, not a movement. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: In Alice in Wonderland, the Mock Turtle's school subjects are jokes. «Reeling and Writhing» is a pun: writhing sounds like writing, and reeling sounds like reading. Puns work because the sounds are almost the same.
explain: If someone is writhing in pain, get help from an adult fast.
fact: Writhing is the -ing form of the verb writhe.
fact: Writhing can describe a person in pain, or a snake or worm wriggling.
fact: «Writhing with embarrassment» means feeling very embarrassed or upset.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, «Reeling and Writhing» is a pun on reading and writing.
fact: If someone is writhing in pain, get help from an adult fast.
exercise: «The snake was writhing in the grass.» What is the snake doing? | Standing very still | Sleeping peacefully | Singing a loud song | *Twisting and wriggling its body
exercise: Mia felt writhing after she tripped in front of the whole class. What does writhing mean here? | Feeling very cold | Feeling very sleepy | Running very fast | *Feeling very embarrassed
exercise: «Reeling and Writhing» is a pun. What school subject does writhing stand for? | Hiding | Drawing | Running | *Writing
test: Sam was writhing on the playground in pain after a fall. What should his friends do first? | Pull him up by his arm | Wait and see if it goes away | *Find a grown-up to help fast | Laugh and walk away
test: In «Reeling and Writhing», what does writhing stand for? | Reading | *Writing | Drawing | Arithmetic
exam: Which word from this lesson means twisting and turning like a snake? | Uglification | Reeling | *Writhing | Ambition
